stment shall be made in the Order price or delivery schedule, or both, and this Order shall be modified in writing accordingly. Any claim by Vendor for adjustment under this clause must be asserted in writing (5) days from the date of receipt by Vendor of the notification of change. Where the cost of property made obsolete or excess as a result of a change is included in Vendors claim for adjustment. Buyer shall have the right to prescribe the manner of disposition of such property. Any charge order issued hereunder will not be binding on Buyer unless issued by an authorized purchasing agent of Buyer. Nothing in this paragraph shall excuse Vendor from proceeding with this Order as changed.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.3529040404040404,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.8897058823529411,"height":0.032196969696969696},"type":"List Item","content":"10. PRICE-If an exact price is not stated in this Order, it is agreed that the goods or services shall be billed at the price last quoted, or billed at the prevailing market price, whichever is lower. This order must not be filled at a higher price than last quoted or charged without Buyer''s specific authorization. Vendor agrees that any price reduction made in the goods and services described in this Order prior to delivery or performance thereof will be applicable to this Order. Vendor represents that the price charged for the goods or services covered by this Order is not more than the lowest price charged by Vendor to buyers of a class similar to Buyer under conditions similar to those specified inthis Order.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.38762626262626265,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.7736928104575164,"height":0.006944444444444444},"type":"List Item","content":"- 11 TAXES-Vendor shall pay all taxes that may arise out of it sales of the goods and services to Buyer. Buyer agrees to pay applicable provincial/state taxes or provide Vendor an exemption certificate.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.39646464646464646,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.8888888888888888,"height":0.05113636363636364},"type":"List Item","content":"- 12 INSPECTION & TESTING-Payment for goods delivered or services rendered hereundershall not constitute acceptance thereof. Buyer shall have the right to inspect such goods or services rendered and to reject any or all of said goods or services which are in Buyer''sjudgmentdefective or nonconforming. Goods rejected and goods suppliedinexcess of quantities called for herein may be returned to Vendorat its risk and expense for full refund, credit or prompt replacement (at Buyer''s option) in addition to Buyer''s other rights. Buyer may charge Vendor all expenses of unpacking, examining, repacking, transportation charges both ways, and similar expenses with respect to such goods. In the event Buyer receives goods or services rendered whose defects or nonconformity is not apparent on examination. Buyer reserves the right to require prompt replacement or correction [in the case of services) as well as payment of damages. Nothing contained in this Order shall relieve in anyway Vendor from the obligation of testing, inspection and quality control. Acceptance of any part of the goods or services shall not bind Buyer to acceptfuture shipments or services, nor deprive it of the right to return goods already accepted if they are defective or nonconforming, or to terminate this Order.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.4494949494949495,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.8888888888888888,"height":0.0422979797979798},"type":"List Item","content":"- 13 DELIVERY & RISK OF LOSS - (i) Vendor agrees to pay all excess charges and expenses resulting from failure to ship and route by cheapest way or as instructed by Buyer, and to reimburse Buyer for any such charges paid or expenses incurred by Buyer for its failure to do so. No charge will be allowed for freight, transportation, insurance, shipping, storage handling, demurrage, cartage, packaging, or similar charges unless provided for in this Order or consented to in writing signed by Buyer. Buyer''s count and weight are to be accepted as final on any shipments. (ii) Risk of loss of any goods furnished pursuant to this Order shall remain on Vendor until such goods are received and accepted by Buyer. (iii) The items on this Order may be used for product manufacturing by Buyer. Therefore, Buyer''s production schedule is based upon quoted delivery or performance dates. By acceptance of this Order, Vendor agrees to be liable for costs that may occur because of delivery or performance time beyond that quoted. Buyer reserves the right to refuse C.O.D. shipments.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.4943181818181818,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.886437908496732,"height":0.032196969696969696},"type":"List Item","content":"14. INSURANCE- In the event that Vendor''s obligations hereunder require or contemplate performance of services by Vendor''s employees, or persons under contract to Vendor to be done on Buyer''s property, or property of Buyer''s customers. Vendor agreed that all such work shall be done as an independent contractor and that the persons doing such work shall not be considered employees or agents of Buyer. Vendor shall maintain all necessary insurance coverage''s, including public liability and Workmen''s Compensation insurance. Vendor shall indemnify and save harmless and defend Buyer from any and all claims or liabilities arising out of work covered by this Paragraph.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.5290404040404041,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.8905228758169934,"height":0.05176767676767677},"type":"List Item","content":"15. BUYER''S PROPERTY-All materials dies, tools, molds, cuts, engravings, etc. supplied by Buyer to Vendor or paid for by Buyer [and any replacements thereof), remain the property of Buyer and unused portion of such materials and such dies, tools, molds, engravings, etc. are to be returned to Buyer immediately, unmodified, at anytime upon demand by Buyer and upon completion of Vendors use thereof, without demand therefore 16. PATENTS-Vendor agrees upon receipt of notification to promptly assume full responsibility for defense of any suit or proceeding which may be brought against Buyer or its agents, customers, or other vendors for alleged patent infringement, as well as for any alleged unfair competition resulting from similarity in design trademark or appearance of goods, or services furnished hereunder, and Vendor further agrees to indemnify Buyer, its agents and customers against any and all expenses, losses, royalties, profits, and damages, including court costs and attorneys'' fees resulting from any such suit or proceeding, including and settlement. Buyer may be represented by and actively participate through its own counsel in any such suit or proceeding if it so desires, and the costs of such representation shall be paid by Vendor.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.5845959595959596,"left":0.02287581699346405,"page":2,"width":0.012254901960784314,"height":0.02904040404040404},"type":"Text","content":"ེ་ཚག","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.5827020202020202,"left":0.056372549019607844,"page":2,"width":0.8308823529411765,"height":0.02462121212121212},"type":"List Item","content":"\\t- PACKAGING- all packaging, packing slips, invoices, correspondence, customs documentation and freight bills of lading shall have the Buyers complete Purchase Order number and part number prominently displayed and packing slips shall accompany all shipments. Invoices will not be processed for payment until all items invoiced are received and approved by the Buyer. GRATUITY-Vendor warrants that neither it nor any of it employees, agents orrepresentatives has offered or given any gratuities to Buyer''s employees agents or representatives.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.6085858585858586,"left":0.05555555555555555,"page":2,"width":0.8602941176470589,"height":0.058712121212121215},"type":"List Item","content":"\\t- PROPRIETARY INFORMATION/CONFIDENTIALITY/ADVERTISING-Vendor shall consider all information furnished by Buyer to be confidential and shall not disclose any such information to any other person, or use such information itself for any purpose other than performing for this Order, unless Vendor obtains written permission from Buyer to do so. This paragraph shall apply to drawings, specifications, or other documents prepared by Vendor for Buyer in connection with thisOrder. Vendor shall not advertiseorpublish the fact that the Buyer hascontractedto purchasegoods or services from Vendor nor shall any informationrelating to this Order be disclosed without Buyer''s priorwritten permission. Unless otherwise agreed in writing no information disclosed in any manneror atany time by Vendor to Buyerin connection with any purchases hereunder shallbe deemed secret, confidential, or proprietary and Vendor shall have no right against Buyer with respect thereto except such rights as may exist under patent law. Vendor acknowledges that trademarks, trade names and trade dress [\\"Marks\\") of Buyer incorporated on or associated with goods supplied by Vendor to Buyer are exclusively owned by Buyer and Vendor will not acquire anyrights to or make any use of such Marks except as expressly permitted herein.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.6704545454545454,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.886437908496732,"height":0.016414141414141416},"type":"List Item","content":"20. INCOMING FREIGHT POLICY-It is Buyer''s policy that incoming freight be \\"F.O.B.\\" Destination or otherwise stated on purchase order, [City and State) freight prepaid and charged back by the supplier on the commodity invoice, charged separately and supported with an original and one copy of freight invoice.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.6887626262626263,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.8880718954248366,"height":0.015151515151515152},"type":"List Item","content":"21. RIGHT OF SETOFF-Buyer specifically reserves the right, in its sole discretion, to set off against amounts to be paid by Buyer to Vendor under its contracts with Vendor, any amounts which Vendor may owe to Buyer, whetherby way of credit, indemnification or otherwise, and whetherpursuant to such contract or any other agreementbetween Buyer and Vendor.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.7058080808080808,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.8790849673202614,"height":0.02462121212121212},"type":"List Item","content":"- 22 FORCE MAEURE- Neither party shall be liable for delay in performanceorfailure to perform (excluding the payment of money) when such delay or failure is due to unforeseen causes beyond its control and without its fault or negligence, including but not limited to acts of God orthe public enemy, government action, fires, floods, earth quakes, epidemics, quarantine restrictions, labor difficulties, riots, insurrections, freight embargoes, plant breakdown, loss of raw material supply, and unusually severe weather.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.7323232323232324,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.6045751633986928,"height":0.006944444444444444},"type":"List Item","content":"- 23 ENTIRE AGREEMENT - this purchase order, and any documents referred to on the face hereof, constitute the entire agreement between the parties.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.7417929292929293,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.8799019607843137,"height":0.015782828282828284},"type":"List Item","content":"- 24 BANKRUPTCY - In the event of any proceeding voluntary or involuntary, in bankruptcy or insolvency by or against the Vendor, including any proceeding under Canadian bankruptcy laws, or in the event of the appointment, with or without Vendor''s consent, of a receiver of an assignee for the benefit of creditors, Buyer shall be entitled to cancel and unfilled part of this Order without any liability whatsoever.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.759469696969697,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.008986928104575163,"height":0.004419191919191919},"type":"Text","content":"25","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.7588383838383839,"left":0.05718954248366013,"page":2,"width":0.7434640522875817,"height":0.007575757575757576},"type":"Text","content":"COMPLIANCE Vendor warrants that all goods and services sold hereunder shall have been produced, sold, delivered and furnished in strict compliance with all applicable laws and regulations.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.7676767676767676,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.8823529411764706,"height":0.015151515151515152},"type":"List Item","content":"26. TRANSPORTATION OF MSDS REQURIED MATERIALS -for all goods or materials subject to Workplace Hazardous Material information System (WHMIS) legislation, Current Material Safety Data Sheets (MSDS) shall accompany the goods or materials and shipping documents.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.7853535353535354,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.8872549019607843,"height":0.015151515151515152},"type":"List Item","content":"27. TRANSPORTATION OF DANGEROUS GOODS-Dangerous goods shall be shipped only in compliance with Canadian Transportation or Dangerous Goods Regulation (TDG), 49 CFR U.S. Hazardous Materials Regulations, and all other environmental laws, rules, regulations and procedures, where applicable.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.803030303030303,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.8880718954248366,"height":0.06818181818181818},"type":"List Item","content":"28. CERTIFIED CANADA CUSTOMS INVOICES AND SHIPPER''S EXPORT DECLARATION-required in quintuple and in addition, commercial invoices in triplicate are to be air mailed to the importer of the day the goods are shipped if goods are moved by rail. When goods are shipped by road transport, Canada Customs invoices and Shipper''s ExportDeclaration in triplicate are to be attached to the carrier''scopy of the bill of lading and sent with the shipment, and an additional two copies and invoices in triplicate, are mailed to the importer. When goods are shipped by air, the customs paper in triplicate are to be attached to the shipment and two additional copies with invoices in triplicate air mailed to importer. Transportation routing must be show on Canada Customs invoices, commercial invoices and bills of lading. The proper commercial description ofthe goods must be given in all invoices. Trade discounts may be allowed and must be deducted on both columns. Cash discount may beshown on invoices but must not be deducted from either column. Invoices must show the marks, the number and the description of the packages in such manner as to indicate truly the quantities and values of articles comprised in each package. In order to facilitate the customs entry of goods from U.S.A., shippers are advised that the way bills should show full information regarding name and address of consignees, marks, numbers and description of packages - that is, whether cases, boxes, pieces, etc. Every piece or case should be numbered consecutively, and if today''s shipments are numbered 1 10, tomorrows should commence with 11, etc.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.8731060606060606,"left":0.056372549019607844,"page":2,"width":0.8390522875816994,"height":0.015782828282828284},"type":"List Item","content":"It is very important that the way bills and bills of lading show the required information in order that the carrier may furnish the reports required to be made at the customs house and prepare manifests for transporting the goods in bond. Buyer will not be responsible for storage or special charges incurred through non-compliance with these instructions and Canada Customs Regulations.","confidence":"high"},{"bbox":{"top":0.8907828282828283,"left":0.02369281045751634,"page":2,"width":0.8921568627450981,"height":0.05808080808080808},"type":"List Item","content":"29 SEVERABILITY- If any provision hereof shall be found to be inoperable orin violation of any law or regulation, only that provision shall be stricken from this order and the remainder of the order shall not be affected. 30. GOVERNING LAW- The laws of the Province of Ontario shall govern this Order and the right and the obligations of the parties hereunder, and the venue of any action brought hereunder shall be in the city of Burlington, Ontario. In the event that Buyer and Vendor are unable to jointly determine and agree, the dispute will be resolved by arbitration using the Canadian Arbitration Association Expedited Arbitration Rules. The parties agree that the Canadian Arbitration Association Expedited Arbitration Rules give the parties a fair opportunity to present their case and respond to the case of the other side. Either party may serve notice of its desire to refer this dispute to arbitration. The arbitration shall be conducted by a single arbitrator. The arbitration shall be held in Burlington, Ontario. The arbitration shall proceed in accordance with the provisions of the Arbitration Act Ontario. The decision arrived at by the arbitrator shall be final and binding and no appeal shall lie there from. Judgment upon the award rendered by the arbitrator may be rendered in any court jurisdiction. The cost of the arbitrator shall be divided equally between Buyer and Vendor.","confidence":"high"}],"content":"[ ]\\n\\nHUNTER\\nAMENITIES\\n\\nPURCHASE ORDER # 2025-00-29652\\n\\nOrdered Date 03/14/2025\\n\\nRevised Date / /\\n\\nTerms: NET 60\\n\\n1205 Corporate Drive Burlington, ON, L7L 5V5 Fax: 905-331-6836 Phone: 905-331-2855\\n\\n\\n\\nIssued To:\\nHanson Chemicals\\n22 Xavier Court\\nBrampton, ON L6Y 5S1\\nAttn: Sweta Patel\\nPH#: 416-457-8271\\nFX#: - - 0\\n\\nShip To:\\nHunter Amenities Burlington.\\n1205 Corporate Drive\\nBurlington, ON. L7L 5V5\\nCurrency: US\\nShip Via: BESTWAY\\nFOB: <empty>\\nAttention:\\n\\n========== ===================\\n\\nDelivery appointments are required for all shipments. Call recieiving at (905-331-2855 ext 268)\\n\\nor e-mail Shiprec@hunteramenities.com\\n\\nHAI purchase order # and part # ''s must appear on all documents\\n\\nGoods to arrive on 40 x 48 pallets, wrapped, clean and free from defect.\\n\\nPlease provide delivery confirmation within 48 hours, thank you.\\n\\n[[\\"Part No.\\", \\"Line\\\\n\\\\nNo.\\", \\"Description\\", \\"Date\\\\nRequired\\", \\"Qty.\\\\nOrdered\\", \\"Unit of\\\\nMeasure\\", \\"Cost\\\\n/Unit:\\", \\"Total Cost:\\"], [\\"C-CHEM7108\\", \\"1 MCT Oil (RSPO) MB\\", \\"1 MCT Oil (RSPO) MB\\", \\"| |\\", \\"15,200.000 Kg\\", \\"15,200.000 Kg\\", \\"5.69000\\", \\"$ 86,488.00\\"], [\\"Freight In-bound\\", \\"2\\", \\"Freight In-bound (65600)\\", \\"\\", \\"15,200.000 EA\\", \\"15,200.000 EA\\", \\"0.29000\\", \\"$ 4,408.00\\"]]\\n\\n## Original\\n\\nAPPROVED BY: Kumari Astuti\\n\\nTotal: $ Total: 90,896.00\\n\\nAcceptance of this order acknowledges\\n\\nPage 1 of 1\\n\\nHunter Amenities Annual Terms and Conditions of Purchase\\n\\n# Terms and Conditions\\n\\n1.\\n\\nACCEPTANCE-(i) This Order is Buyer''s offer to Vendor. Any reference to any offer to sell, quotation or proposal of incorporating the description and specifications of the goods and services contained there in to the extent they do not conflict with those contained in this order. (ii) By acknowledging receipt of this Order (or by shipping the goods or performing the services called for by this Order) Vendor agrees to the terms and conditions contained herein. It is agreed that any additional or different terms or conditions contained in any acknowledgement of this Order or other document furnished by Vendor are waived by Vendor and shall be deemed objected to by Buyer without need of further notice of objection and shall be of no effect nor in any circumstance binding upon Buyer unless accepted by Buyer in writing. (iii) The face and reverse of this Purchase Order, and any documents attached hereto, referred to on the face hereof or incorporated by reference herein, including any specifications, drawings and data submitted to Vendor by or on behalf of Buyer, constitute the entire agreement between the parties (collectively the \\"Order]\\n\\n2. PAYMENT - Discount terms are as set forth on the purchase order. If no terms are specified, the net amount shall be payable within 60 days from delivery and acceptance of goods. Unless expressly otherwise, Buyer shall not be liable for any shipping, handling, fuel surcharges or similar fees.\\n\\n3. ASSIGNMENT & SUBCONTRACTING- Vendor shall not assign this Order or any of its rights hereunder or subcontract any portion of the work hereunder without prior written consent of Buyer, and any purposed assignment or subcontracting without Buyer''s prior written consent shall be void.\\n\\n4. TIME OF ESSENCE - Time(s) of shipment, rendering of services and quantities and qualities specified are of the essence. Vendor shall promptly notify Buyer whenever it appears to Vendor that it will not be able to deliver as specified. Buyer, at its option may take steps to assist Vendor in expediting delivery to Vendor of anything necessary for Vendors timely performance of its obligations hereunder, inwhich case any excess costs incurred by reason of the expected delivery shall be paid by Vendor.\\n\\n5.\\n\\nTERMINATION – Without prejudice to any other rights or remedies Buyer may cancel this Order in whole or in part if the goods and services are defective or nonconforming or are not delivered or perform edas scheduled or if Vendor fails to comply with any of the terms and conditions hereof which termination will be without any liability of Buyer except for payment due for goods and services delivered to and accepted by Buyer. Buyer may also cancel this Order in whole or in part at its convenience, upon written or oral notice to Vendor, in which event Vendors sole remedy shall be limited to recovery of reasonable charges reflecting the portion of the work performed prior to termination plus actual direct documented costs resulting from termination. Upon cancellation of this Order for any reason, Vendor will stop work on the date and to the extent specified in any notice of cancellation and terminate all orders that relate to the terminated order.\\n\\n6. WARRANTY - Vendor warrants that the goods furnished hereunder will (i) befree and clear of all liens, encumbrances and interests of any other person or entity, (ii) be free from defects in workmanship and material, (ii) be free from defects in design, (iv) be suitable for the purposes intended, (v) be in compliance with all requirements of this Order and all applicable drawings, specifications, samples, representations or other descriptions and (vi) not infringe any rights of any third parties relating to patents, trademarks, design, appearance or other intellectual property rights (except for infringement arising due to Buyer''s specifications or matter provided by Buyer for use or inclusion with goods). All warranties both expressed and implied, shall inure to Buyer, its customers and end users. Vendor further warrants that all services performed for or on behalf of Buyer will be performed in a competent, workmanlike manner, shall be free from faults and defects, and shall conform to all of Buyer''s instructions, specifications, and directions. 7. CHEMICALSANDFRAGRANCES SHELF LIFE Every material received should have 75% ofshelf life from the date received into Hunter Amenities. For chemicals contracted annually, the shelf life has to be within the contract period, but not less than 100 days from the day the material is received at our dock.\\n\\n8.\\n\\nINDEMNITY-Vendor agrees to indemnify, defend and forever hold Buyer and Buyer''s affiliates, parents, subsidiaries, vendees, officers, directors, employees, agents, successors and assigns harmless from and against any and all losses, liabilities, claims, costs, damages, fees and expenses (including, but not limited to, penalties, fines, forfeitures, reasonable attorneys fees, disbursements and administrative or court costs) [\\"Losses\\") relating to this Order (including any breech of Vendor representations hereunder) orgoods or services purchased hereunder (including actual or alleged product or manufacturingdefects or nonconformities, defects or nonconformities, defects or nonconformities in services or failure to timely perform Vendors obligations hereunder), infringement or violation of third-party rights related to the foregoing, and any other acts or omissions by Vendor, its agents, employees, or subcontractors related to the foregoing (including acts or omissions resulting in any claim for injuries or damage to any person or property).\\n\\nCHANGES- Buyer may at anytime, by written order, make changes within the generalscope of this Order in any one or more of the following: (i) drawings, designs or specifications, where the materialsto befurnished are to be specifically manufactured in accordance therewith, (ii) method of shipment or packaging, [iii] places of delivery, (iv) delivery dates and, (v) quantities. If any such change causes an increase or decrease in the cost of, or the time required for the performance of any part of the work to be performed hereunder, an equitable adjustment shall be made in the Order price or delivery schedule, or both, and this Order shall be modified in writing accordingly. Any claim by Vendor for adjustment under this clause must be asserted in writing (5) days from the date of receipt by Vendor of the notification of change. Where the cost of property made obsolete or excess as a result of a change is included in Vendors claim for adjustment. Buyer shall have the right to prescribe the manner of disposition of such property. Any charge order issued hereunder will not be binding on Buyer unless issued by an authorized purchasing agent of Buyer. Nothing in this paragraph shall excuse Vendor from proceeding with this Order as changed.\\n\\n10. PRICE-If an exact price is not stated in this Order, it is agreed that the goods or services shall be billed at the price last quoted, or billed at the prevailing market price, whichever is lower. This order must not be filled at a higher price than last quoted or charged without Buyer''s specific authorization. Vendor agrees that any price reduction made in the goods and services described in this Order prior to delivery or performance thereof will be applicable to this Order. Vendor represents that the price charged for the goods or services covered by this Order is not more than the lowest price charged by Vendor to buyers of a class similar to Buyer under conditions similar to those specified inthis Order.\\n\\n- 11 TAXES-Vendor shall pay all taxes that may arise out of it sales of the goods and services to Buyer. Buyer agrees to pay applicable provincial/state taxes or provide Vendor an exemption certificate.\\n\\n- 12 INSPECTION & TESTING-Payment for goods delivered or services rendered hereundershall not constitute acceptance thereof. Buyer shall have the right to inspect such goods or services rendered and to reject any or all of said goods or services which are in Buyer''sjudgmentdefective or nonconforming. Goods rejected and goods suppliedinexcess of quantities called for herein may be returned to Vendorat its risk and expense for full refund, credit or prompt replacement (at Buyer''s option) in addition to Buyer''s other rights. Buyer may charge Vendor all expenses of unpacking, examining, repacking, transportation charges both ways, and similar expenses with respect to such goods. In the event Buyer receives goods or services rendered whose defects or nonconformity is not apparent on examination. Buyer reserves the right to require prompt replacement or correction [in the case of services) as well as payment of damages. Nothing contained in this Order shall relieve in anyway Vendor from the obligation of testing, inspection and quality control. Acceptance of any part of the goods or services shall not bind Buyer to acceptfuture shipments or services, nor deprive it of the right to return goods already accepted if they are defective or nonconforming, or to terminate this Order.\\n\\n- 13 DELIVERY & RISK OF LOSS - (i) Vendor agrees to pay all excess charges and expenses resulting from failure to ship and route by cheapest way or as instructed by Buyer, and to reimburse Buyer for any such charges paid or expenses incurred by Buyer for its failure to do so. No charge will be allowed for freight, transportation, insurance, shipping, storage handling, demurrage, cartage, packaging, or similar charges unless provided for in this Order or consented to in writing signed by Buyer. Buyer''s count and weight are to be accepted as final on any shipments. (ii) Risk of loss of any goods furnished pursuant to this Order shall remain on Vendor until such goods are received and accepted by Buyer. (iii) The items on this Order may be used for product manufacturing by Buyer. Therefore, Buyer''s production schedule is based upon quoted delivery or performance dates. By acceptance of this Order, Vendor agrees to be liable for costs that may occur because of delivery or performance time beyond that quoted. Buyer reserves the right to refuse C.O.D. shipments.\\n\\n14. INSURANCE- In the event that Vendor''s obligations hereunder require or contemplate performance of services by Vendor''s employees, or persons under contract to Vendor to be done on Buyer''s property, or property of Buyer''s customers. Vendor agreed that all such work shall be done as an independent contractor and that the persons doing such work shall not be considered employees or agents of Buyer. Vendor shall maintain all necessary insurance coverage''s, including public liability and Workmen''s Compensation insurance. Vendor shall indemnify and save harmless and defend Buyer from any and all claims or liabilities arising out of work covered by this Paragraph.\\n\\n15. BUYER''S PROPERTY-All materials dies, tools, molds, cuts, engravings, etc. supplied by Buyer to Vendor or paid for by Buyer [and any replacements thereof), remain the property of Buyer and unused portion of such materials and such dies, tools, molds, engravings, etc. are to be returned to Buyer immediately, unmodified, at anytime upon demand by Buyer and upon completion of Vendors use thereof, without demand therefore 16. PATENTS-Vendor agrees upon receipt of notification to promptly assume full responsibility for defense of any suit or proceeding which may be brought against Buyer or its agents, customers, or other vendors for alleged patent infringement, as well as for any alleged unfair competition resulting from similarity in design trademark or appearance of goods, or services furnished hereunder, and Vendor further agrees to indemnify Buyer, its agents and customers against any and all expenses, losses, royalties, profits, and damages, including court costs and attorneys'' fees resulting from any such suit or proceeding, including and settlement. Buyer may be represented by and actively participate through its own counsel in any such suit or proceeding if it so desires, and the costs of such representation shall be paid by Vendor.\\n\\nེ་ཚག\\n\\n\\t- PACKAGING- all packaging, packing slips, invoices, correspondence, customs documentation and freight bills of lading shall have the Buyers complete Purchase Order number and part number prominently displayed and packing slips shall accompany all shipments. Invoices will not be processed for payment until all items invoiced are received and approved by the Buyer. GRATUITY-Vendor warrants that neither it nor any of it employees, agents orrepresentatives has offered or given any gratuities to Buyer''s employees agents or representatives.\\n\\n\\t- PROPRIETARY INFORMATION/CONFIDENTIALITY/ADVERTISING-Vendor shall consider all information furnished by Buyer to be confidential and shall not disclose any such information to any other person, or use such information itself for any purpose other than performing for this Order, unless Vendor obtains written permission from Buyer to do so. This paragraph shall apply to drawings, specifications, or other documents prepared by Vendor for Buyer in connection with thisOrder. Vendor shall not advertiseorpublish the fact that the Buyer hascontractedto purchasegoods or services from Vendor nor shall any informationrelating to this Order be disclosed without Buyer''s priorwritten permission. Unless otherwise agreed in writing no information disclosed in any manneror atany time by Vendor to Buyerin connection with any purchases hereunder shallbe deemed secret, confidential, or proprietary and Vendor shall have no right against Buyer with respect thereto except such rights as may exist under patent law. Vendor acknowledges that trademarks, trade names and trade dress [\\"Marks\\") of Buyer incorporated on or associated with goods supplied by Vendor to Buyer are exclusively owned by Buyer and Vendor will not acquire anyrights to or make any use of such Marks except as expressly permitted herein.\\n\\n20. INCOMING FREIGHT POLICY-It is Buyer''s policy that incoming freight be \\"F.O.B.\\" Destination or otherwise stated on purchase order, [City and State) freight prepaid and charged back by the supplier on the commodity invoice, charged separately and supported with an original and one copy of freight invoice.\\n\\n21. RIGHT OF SETOFF-Buyer specifically reserves the right, in its sole discretion, to set off against amounts to be paid by Buyer to Vendor under its contracts with Vendor, any amounts which Vendor may owe to Buyer, whetherby way of credit, indemnification or otherwise, and whetherpursuant to such contract or any other agreementbetween Buyer and Vendor.\\n\\n- 22 FORCE MAEURE- Neither party shall be liable for delay in performanceorfailure to perform (excluding the payment of money) when such delay or failure is due to unforeseen causes beyond its control and without its fault or negligence, including but not limited to acts of God orthe public enemy, government action, fires, floods, earth quakes, epidemics, quarantine restrictions, labor difficulties, riots, insurrections, freight embargoes, plant breakdown, loss of raw material supply, and unusually severe weather.\\n\\n- 23 ENTIRE AGREEMENT - this purchase order, and any documents referred to on the face hereof, constitute the entire agreement between the parties.\\n\\n- 24 BANKRUPTCY - In the event of any proceeding voluntary or involuntary, in bankruptcy or insolvency by or against the Vendor, including any proceeding under Canadian bankruptcy laws, or in the event of the appointment, with or without Vendor''s consent, of a receiver of an assignee for the benefit of creditors, Buyer shall be entitled to cancel and unfilled part of this Order without any liability whatsoever.\\n\\n25\\n\\nCOMPLIANCE Vendor warrants that all goods and services sold hereunder shall have been produced, sold, delivered and furnished in strict compliance with all applicable laws and regulations.\\n\\n26. TRANSPORTATION OF MSDS REQURIED MATERIALS -for all goods or materials subject to Workplace Hazardous Material information System (WHMIS) legislation, Current Material Safety Data Sheets (MSDS) shall accompany the goods or materials and shipping documents.\\n\\n27. TRANSPORTATION OF DANGEROUS GOODS-Dangerous goods shall be shipped only in compliance with Canadian Transportation or Dangerous Goods Regulation (TDG), 49 CFR U.S. Hazardous Materials Regulations, and all other environmental laws, rules, regulations and procedures, where applicable.\\n\\n28. CERTIFIED CANADA CUSTOMS INVOICES AND SHIPPER''S EXPORT DECLARATION-required in quintuple and in addition, commercial invoices in triplicate are to be air mailed to the importer of the day the goods are shipped if goods are moved by rail. When goods are shipped by road transport, Canada Customs invoices and Shipper''s ExportDeclaration in triplicate are to be attached to the carrier''scopy of the bill of lading and sent with the shipment, and an additional two copies and invoices in triplicate, are mailed to the importer. When goods are shipped by air, the customs paper in triplicate are to be attached to the shipment and two additional copies with invoices in triplicate air mailed to importer. Transportation routing must be show on Canada Customs invoices, commercial invoices and bills of lading. The proper commercial description ofthe goods must be given in all invoices. Trade discounts may be allowed and must be deducted on both columns. Cash discount may beshown on invoices but must not be deducted from either column. Invoices must show the marks, the number and the description of the packages in such manner as to indicate truly the quantities and values of articles comprised in each package. In order to facilitate the customs entry of goods from U.S.A., shippers are advised that the way bills should show full information regarding name and address of consignees, marks, numbers and description of packages - that is, whether cases, boxes, pieces, etc. Every piece or case should be numbered consecutively, and if today''s shipments are numbered 1 10, tomorrows should commence with 11, etc.\\n\\nIt is very important that the way bills and bills of lading show the required information in order that the carrier may furnish the reports required to be made at the customs house and prepare manifests for transporting the goods in bond. Buyer will not be responsible for storage or special charges incurred through non-compliance with these instructions and Canada Customs Regulations.\\n\\n29 SEVERABILITY- If any provision hereof shall be found to be inoperable orin violation of any law or regulation, only that provision shall be stricken from this order and the remainder of the order shall not be affected. 30. GOVERNING LAW- The laws of the Province of Ontario shall govern this Order and the right and the obligations of the parties hereunder, and the venue of any action brought hereunder shall be in the city of Burlington, Ontario. In the event that Buyer and Vendor are unable to jointly determine and agree, the dispute will be resolved by arbitration using the Canadian Arbitration Association Expedited Arbitration Rules. The parties agree that the Canadian Arbitration Association Expedited Arbitration Rules give the parties a fair opportunity to present their case and respond to the case of the other side. Either party may serve notice of its desire to refer this dispute to arbitration. The arbitration shall be conducted by a single arbitrator. The arbitration shall be held in Burlington, Ontario. The arbitration shall proceed in accordance with the provisions of the Arbitration Act Ontario. The decision arrived at by the arbitrator shall be final and binding and no appeal shall lie there from. Judgment upon the award rendered by the arbitrator may be rendered in any court jurisdiction. The cost of the arbitrator shall be divided equally between Buyer and Vendor."}],"job_id":"c3d1f866-071c-4ac9-84a1-20ce0e595abd","duration":9.997992753982544,"studio_link":"https://studio.reducto.ai/job/c3d1f866-071c-4ac9-84a1-20ce0e595abd"}', 'processed', '2026-01-13 01:47:59.376374+00', '2026-01-13 01:50:11.174336+00', '{"bol_number": "2026011303", "bol_date": "2026-01-13", "ship_from": {"name": "Hanson Chemicals", "address": "22 Xavier Court", "city": "Brampton", "state": "ON", "zip_code": "L6Y 5S1", "country": "CANADA", "phone": "416-475-8271", "email": "spatel@hansonchemicals.com"}, "ship_to": {"name": "Hunter Amenities Burlington.", "address": "1205 Corporate Drive", "city": "Burlington", "state": "ON", "zip_code": "L7L 5V5", "country": "CANADA", "phone": "905-331-2855", "email": "Shiprec@hunteramenities.com"}, "bill_to": null, "products": [{"name": "MCT Oil (RSPO) MB", "des